{"format":"chroniques-modele-campagne","version":1,"exportedAt":"2026-11-27T00:00:00.000Z","title":"The Drowned Lantern — starter adventure","edition":"","adventure":{"lang":"en","notes":"Starter adventure for 3 to 5 level 1 characters (2 to 3 hours). Original text for Chroniques; creatures from the SRD 5.1 (CC BY 4.0)."},"planner":{"places":[{"id":"cp-advplace0000","title":"Saltport","summary":"Small fog-bound fishing harbour at the foot of Greypoint. An inn, the Jolly Cod, a quay and some fifty houses.","privateNotes":"The fishers are scared: three nights without a lighthouse and a boat smashed on the reef. They talk freely for a round of drinks.","context":"Greypoint coast","visibility":"shared","status":"","date":""},{"id":"cp-advplace1000","title":"Greypoint Lighthouse","summary":"White stone tower at the end of the headland. Its lantern guides boats between the reefs.","privateNotes":"The lens has been taken off and carried away. A trapdoor under the rug in the ground-floor room leads to carved stairs going down to the cave.","context":"Greypoint","visibility":"shared","status":"","date":""},{"id":"cp-advplace2000","title":"The Wreckers’ Cave","summary":"Sea cave beneath the lighthouse, opening onto a cove.","privateNotes":"Corbin’s den: campfire, loot from the wrecks, a rowing boat. Maëlle is locked in a cage at the back, on the left.","context":"Beneath the lighthouse","visibility":"private","status":"","date":""},{"id":"cp-advplace3000","title":"The Crypt of the Drowned","summary":"Old crypt where the village once laid sailors lost at sea.","privateNotes":"While digging around, the wreckers woke three skeletons. The lens is hidden there, in a chest at the foot of the altar.","context":"Beneath the cave","visibility":"private","status":"","date":""}],"quests":[{"id":"cp-advquest0000","title":"Relight the lighthouse","summary":"Greypoint lighthouse has gone dark and its keeper has vanished. The Saltport council offers 50 gp to bring the light back.","privateNotes":"Real cause: Corbin’s wreckers. Finding Maëlle and the lens is enough to relight the lighthouse.","context":"Saltport","visibility":"shared","status":"active","date":"","objectives":[{"id":"obj-advq00000","text":"Talk to the harbour folk","secret":false},{"id":"obj-advq10000","text":"Search the lighthouse","secret":false},{"id":"obj-advq20000","text":"Find Maëlle Ressac","secret":false},{"id":"obj-advq30000","text":"Recover the lighthouse lens","secret":false},{"id":"obj-advq40000","text":"Find out who buys Corbin’s loot","secret":true}]}],"npcs":[{"id":"cp-advnpc00000","title":"Maëlle Ressac","summary":"Lighthouse keeper, forty, calloused hands and a voice like a storm.","privateNotes":"Held prisoner by the wreckers. She knows Corbin sells the loot to someone called “Aubry”, a merchant in town. Reward: she gives away her old spyglass (an ordinary item, very handy).","context":"Wreckers’ Cave","visibility":"shared","status":"","date":"","attitude":"amical"},{"id":"cp-advnpc01000","title":"Yann Kerbriand","summary":"Landlord of the Jolly Cod, a chatty former fisher.","privateNotes":"Offers 50 gp on behalf of the harbour council. He saw lights moving on the cliff the night of the wreck.","context":"Saltport","visibility":"shared","status":"","date":"","attitude":"amical"},{"id":"cp-advnpc02000","title":"Corbin the Grey","summary":"Former smuggler in a faded coat.","privateNotes":"He puts out the lighthouse and waves false lanterns from the cliff to lure boats onto the reef. A coward: he bargains or runs rather than die.","context":"Wreckers’ Cave","visibility":"private","status":"","date":"","attitude":"hostile"}],"factions":[],"treasures":[],"sessions":[],"journal":[]},"scenes":[{"id":"sc-advscene0000","title":"Arriving in Saltport","summary":"The characters reach the harbour and hear about the missing keeper and the council’s offer.","readAloud":"Fog clings to the slate roofs and the smell of dried fish drifts all the way to the road. At the end of the headland, the white shape of the lighthouse stands against the grey sky… but its lantern is dead. On the quay, fishers silently mend what is left of a boat split in two.","gmNotes":"Hook: Yann Kerbriand, at the inn, offers 50 gp. Rumours: use the “Harbour rumours” table. Clue to reveal: the lights on the cliff. Hand out the council notice.","status":"planned","visibility":"private","links":[{"type":"places","id":"cp-advplace0000"},{"type":"npcs","id":"cp-advnpc01000"},{"type":"quests","id":"cp-advquest0000"}]},{"id":"sc-advscene1000","title":"The cliff path","summary":"A narrow path runs along the sea to the lighthouse.","readAloud":"The wind whistles between the rocks. Below, waves lap a pebble beach where something stirs under the sand. Higher up, an unlit lantern hangs from a hook driven into the rock, facing out to sea.","gmNotes":"Two possible encounters: the crabs on the beach, the lookouts further up. The hook and lantern are a clue: someone lights up the sea from here.","status":"planned","visibility":"private","links":[{"type":"encounters","id":"enc-advplage000"},{"type":"encounters","id":"enc-advguet0000"}]},{"id":"sc-advscene2000","title":"The dark lighthouse","summary":"The ground-floor room is a mess; the lens is gone.","readAloud":"The lighthouse door bangs in the wind. Inside: overturned chairs, a broken cup, and on the table the keeper’s logbook, open at the last page. At the very top, the great glass lens has been torn from its mount.","gmNotes":"Wisdom (Perception) check DC 12: the trapdoor under the rug. Hand out the page from Maëlle’s log. The rats are in the storeroom.","status":"planned","visibility":"private","links":[{"type":"places","id":"cp-advplace1000"},{"type":"encounters","id":"enc-advrats0000"}]},{"id":"sc-advscene3000","title":"The Wreckers’ Cave","summary":"Corbin’s den, his loot and his prisoner.","readAloud":"The carved stairs open onto a vast cavern. A fire crackles among split crates, and the black water of a cove slaps against a jetty. Laughter stops dead: they heard you.","gmNotes":"Map “Wreckers’ Cave”. Corbin bargains if things go badly. His notebook is in his jacket. Maëlle is in the cage (key on Corbin, or Strength DC 13).","status":"planned","visibility":"private","links":[{"type":"places","id":"cp-advplace2000"},{"type":"npcs","id":"cp-advnpc02000"},{"type":"encounters","id":"enc-advrepaire0"}]},{"id":"sc-advscene4000","title":"The Crypt of the Drowned","summary":"Optional: the lens hidden at the back of the crypt.","readAloud":"Beneath the cave, worn steps lead down to a cold chamber. Niches cut in the stone hold bones wrapped in fishing nets. At the foot of an altar covered in shells, a brand-new chest looks out of place.","gmNotes":"Hard encounter for level 1 characters: let them choose to rest first (short rest). The lens is in the chest.","status":"planned","visibility":"private","links":[{"type":"places","id":"cp-advplace3000"},{"type":"encounters","id":"enc-advcrypte00"}]},{"id":"sc-advscene5000","title":"Epilogue: the light returns","summary":"With the lens back in place, the lighthouse shines again.","readAloud":"When the flame leaps up behind the glass, a golden beam sweeps across the sea and the fog. On the quay, someone gives a cry of joy, then the whole harbour starts to cheer.","gmNotes":"Rewards: 50 gp from the council, Maëlle’s spyglass, the cave loot. Lead for what comes next: “Aubry”, the buyer of the loot.","status":"planned","visibility":"private","links":[{"type":"quests","id":"cp-advquest0000"},{"type":"npcs","id":"cp-advnpc00000"}]}],"templates":[{"id":"tpl-advcrab0001","srd":"giant-crab","name":"Giant Crab","kind":"monstre","hpMax":13,"ac":15,"initiative":2,"speed":9,"visibility":"hidden","showHp":false,"actions":"Claw: Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 11). The crab has two claws, each of which can grapple only one target.","notes":"SRD bestiary (CC BY 4.0): Bête, CR 1/8.","traits":"Speed: swim 30 ft.. · Amphibious: The crab can breathe air and water.","legendary":"","defenses":{},"abilities":{"str":13,"dex":15,"con":11,"int":1,"wis":9,"cha":3},"cr":"1/8","spellcasting":null,"icon":""},{"id":"tpl-advband0001","srd":"bandit","name":"Bandit","kind":"monstre","hpMax":11,"ac":12,"initiative":1,"speed":9,"visibility":"hidden","showHp":false,"actions":"Scimitar: Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) slashing damage. Light Crossbow: Ranged Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage.","notes":"SRD bestiary (CC BY 4.0): Humanoïde, CR 1/8.","traits":"","legendary":"","defenses":{},"abilities":{"str":11,"dex":12,"con":12,"int":10,"wis":10,"cha":10},"cr":"1/8","spellcasting":null,"icon":""},{"id":"tpl-advrats0001","srd":"swarm-of-rats","name":"Swarm of Rats","kind":"monstre","hpMax":24,"ac":10,"initiative":0,"speed":9,"visibility":"hidden","showHp":false,"actions":"Bites: Melee Weapon Attack: +2 to hit, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 7 (2d6) piercing damage, or 3 (1d6) piercing damage if the swarm has half of its hit points or fewer.","notes":"SRD bestiary (CC BY 4.0): Nuée de bêtes, CR 1/4.","traits":"Keen Smell: The swarm has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell. · Swarm: The swarm can occupy another creature's space and vice versa, and the swarm can move through any opening large enough for a Tiny rat. The swarm can't regain hit points or gain temporary hit points.","legendary":"","defenses":{"Contondant":"resist","Perforant":"resist","Tranchant":"resist"},"abilities":{"str":9,"dex":11,"con":9,"int":2,"wis":10,"cha":3},"cr":"1/4","spellcasting":null,"icon":""},{"id":"tpl-advskel0001","srd":"skeleton","name":"Skeleton","kind":"monstre","hpMax":13,"ac":13,"initiative":2,"speed":9,"visibility":"hidden","showHp":false,"actions":"Shortsword: Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage. Shortbow: Ranged Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.","notes":"SRD bestiary (CC BY 4.0): Mort-vivant, CR 1/4.","traits":"","legendary":"","defenses":{"Contondant":"vuln","Poison":"immune"},"abilities":{"str":10,"dex":14,"con":15,"int":6,"wis":8,"cha":5},"cr":"1/4","spellcasting":null,"icon":""},{"id":"tpl-advcorb0001","srd":"","name":"Corbin the Grey","kind":"monstre","hpMax":22,"ac":14,"initiative":1,"speed":9,"visibility":"hidden","showHp":false,"actions":"Cutlass: +4 to hit, 1d6+2 slashing. Light crossbow: +4 (80/320 ft), 1d8+2 piercing. Two attacks per turn.","notes":"Leader of the wreckers. Flees to the rowing boat if reduced below 8 HP. Built on the SRD Bandit, toughened up.","traits":"Dirty trick (once per combat): when a creature misses him in melee, he throws sand in its eyes; it has disadvantage on its next attack.","legendary":"","defenses":{},"abilities":{"str":12,"dex":14,"con":12,"int":11,"wis":10,"cha":13},"cr":"1/2","spellcasting":null,"icon":""}],"encounters":[{"id":"enc-advplage000","name":"Beach crabs","notes":"Two giant crabs burst out of the sand at the bottom of the path. Easy: a warm-up.","groups":[{"id":"grp-advplag0000","templateId":"tpl-advcrab0001","quantity":2}]},{"id":"enc-advguet0000","name":"Cliff lookouts","notes":"Two wreckers watch the path. If they spot the characters, one runs to warn Corbin.","groups":[{"id":"grp-advguet0000","templateId":"tpl-advband0001","quantity":2}]},{"id":"enc-advrats0000","name":"Rat cellar","notes":"A swarm of rats in the lighthouse storeroom, drawn by Maëlle’s supplies.","groups":[{"id":"grp-advrats0000","templateId":"tpl-advrats0001","quantity":1}]},{"id":"enc-advrepaire0","name":"Corbin’s den","notes":"Corbin and two wreckers around the fire. If the lookout raised the alarm, they wait behind the crates (half cover).","groups":[{"id":"grp-advrepa0000","templateId":"tpl-advcorb0001","quantity":1},{"id":"grp-advrepa1000","templateId":"tpl-advband0001","quantity":2}]},{"id":"enc-advcrypte00","name":"Drowned guardians","notes":"Three skeletons in sailors’ rags rise when someone approaches the altar. Optional, hard encounter: they don’t follow beyond the stairs.","groups":[{"id":"grp-advcryp0000","templateId":"tpl-advskel0001","quantity":3}]}],"items":[{"id":"hb-advlens0001","name":"Greypoint lens","description":"The lighthouse’s great lens of cut glass, heavy and fragile. Not magical, but irreplaceable for the village.","notes":"Given back to Maëlle, it relights the lighthouse.","category":"treasure","rarity":"","attunement":false,"weight":5,"chargesMax":0,"icon":""}],"handouts":[{"id":"doc-advdoc0000","title":"Notice from the Saltport council","text":"Greypoint lighthouse has been dark for three nights and its keeper, Maëlle Ressac, has not been seen since.\n\nThe council offers FIFTY GOLD PIECES to whoever brings the light back.\n\nAsk for Yann Kerbriand at the Jolly Cod."},{"id":"doc-advdoc1000","title":"Page from Maëlle’s log","text":"Third night in a row I’ve seen a light on the cliff, where nobody should be. Tonight I’ll go and look. If I don’t come back, don’t let the lighthouse stay dark.\n\n— M. R."},{"id":"doc-advdoc2000","title":"Corbin’s notebook","text":"Lens: hidden down below, with the Drowned. Nobody will look for it there.\nNext load for Aubry: silks and two barrels of brandy. He pays at the new moon, same place.\nThe keeper: keep her quiet until the next ship."}],"clues":[{"id":"clue-advc0000","title":"Lights on the cliff","text":"On the night of the wreck, several fishers saw lights moving on the cliff, far from the lighthouse.","gmNote":"The wreckers wave false lanterns to lure boats onto the reef.","tag":"indice"},{"id":"clue-advc1000","title":"The hook in the rock","text":"A lantern hangs from a hook driven into the cliff, facing out to sea.","gmNote":"Proof that someone lights up the sea from the path.","tag":"indice"},{"id":"clue-advc2000","title":"Who buys the loot?","text":"Corbin’s notebook mentions someone called “Aubry” who pays at the new moon.","gmNote":"Lead for a sequel: Aubry, a respectable merchant in town.","tag":"question"}],"shops":[],"loot":[{"id":"loot-advloot001","name":"Cave loot","description":"60 gp, silks (worth 25 gp) and a potion of healing in the crates.","category":"treasure","quantity":1,"weight":0}],"tables":[{"id":"rt-advrumor001","name":"Harbour rumours","die":"d6","category":"","visibility":"private","notes":"","rows":[{"min":1,"max":1,"text":"The keeper threw herself into the sea out of grief. (false)"},{"min":2,"max":2,"text":"Lights were seen on the cliff the night of the wreck. (true)"},{"min":3,"max":3,"text":"A merchant in town buys everything the sea washes up. (true)"},{"min":4,"max":4,"text":"The drowned walk out of the old crypt on moonless nights. (partly true)"},{"min":5,"max":5,"text":"Corbin the Grey, the old smuggler, is back in the area. (true)"},{"min":6,"max":6,"text":"The lighthouse has been cursed since its lens was changed. (false)"}]}],"houseRules":[],"maps":[{"id":"map-advgrotte01","title":"Wreckers’ Cave","summary":"Sea cave beneath the lighthouse.","visibility":"private","grid":{"cells":30,"scale":"5 ft"},"image":{"mime":"image/webp","base64":""},"markers":[{"id":"pin-advpin0000","title":"Stair entrance","description":"Arrival from the lighthouse trapdoor.","visibility":"private","x":90,"y":830,"symbol":"place","linked":null,"builtin":null},{"id":"pin-advpin1000","title":"Campfire","description":"Corbin and his men.","visibility":"private","x":388,"y":595,"symbol":"monster","linked":null,"builtin":null},{"id":"pin-advpin2000","title":"Maëlle’s cage","description":"Key on Corbin, or Strength DC 13.","visibility":"private","x":140,"y":210,"symbol":"npc","linked":null,"builtin":null},{"id":"pin-advpin3000","title":"Loot crates","description":"60 gp, silks, a potion of healing.","visibility":"private","x":460,"y":360,"symbol":"chest","linked":null,"builtin":null},{"id":"pin-advpin4000","title":"Jetty and boat","description":"Corbin’s escape route.","visibility":"private","x":780,"y":610,"symbol":"point","linked":null,"builtin":null},{"id":"pin-advpin5000","title":"Crypt stairs","description":"Down to the Crypt of the Drowned.","visibility":"private","x":782,"y":120,"symbol":"portal","linked":null,"builtin":null}]}]}
